{"title":"2026 CEMC Euclid Problem 6B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Euclid_Problem_6B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, quadilateral ABCD has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/5777c79e87f3d5971731def57ae2d0da562eccd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6390d4c4313a6fd3f94951462bf2f74e1cbc83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba9c5b794a65e12cd362d3f8a7a5873d1585f2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDA = 135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />. Determine the exact value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31a62261a99d8f1d570a28f47f9fdffa86f51f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC - CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f2b02ad1bfe2225c12a08eeb3ae06b38b5aab4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; import graph; size(250); // Controls the display size of the diagram  // Define the exact coordinates based on the geometric properties pair A = (0, 0); pair D = (4, 0); pair B = 4 * dir(120); // AB = 4 at a 120-degree angle pair C = (2 + 2*sqrt(3), 2*sqrt(3) - 2);  // Draw the quadrilateral segments draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(1.2bp));  // Label the vertices with correct padding directions label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"215\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Euclid_Problem_6B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we connect AC to form two triangles.\n</p><p>Next, we , let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b13a806ee59da256367d4cbdb66f73a22533c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55baada2ecf6cca2503bd8e53c56391fb80b77f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81729679b37323d6005b4977da289885085b703.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; import graph; size(250); pair A = (0, 0); pair D = (4, 0); pair B = 4 * dir(120);  pair C = (2 + 2*sqrt(3), 2*sqrt(3) - 2); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(1.2bp)); draw(A--C, linewidth(0.9bp));  label(&quot;$x$&quot;, (B+C)/2, NE); label(&quot;$y$&quot;, (C+D)/2, NE); label(&quot;$45^\\circ$&quot;, B + 0.8*dir(-37.5)); label(&quot;$135^\\circ$&quot;, D + 0.7*dir(112.5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"215\" />\n</p><p>Applying the law of cosine in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4efeb9b1f073b9a156606d1c7cef944c4df07016.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = AB^2 + BC^2 - 2(AB)(BC)\\cos(45^\\circ)\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc6d1291e2154308bcd37e89c35453209ab441e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = 16 + x^2 - 8x\\cos(45^\\circ)\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18cdd49205935619aa474dff1f4dffc983a2ed3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = 16 + x^2 - 4x\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Applying the law of cosine in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a47805c7c3702c1dde23646010394d1bf576e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = AD^2 + CD^2 - 2(AD)(CD)\\cos(135^\\circ)\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f465286021479c3dff90873b25c1a5c0f9feb3fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = 16 + y^2 - 8y\\cos(135^\\circ)\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/7597d8b8d80c60b31463c57ce8e2858f70444d51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2 = 16 + y^2 + 4y\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Connecting the two equations, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f913b561683f24d8683906631351ed0a1c50bac3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 + x^2 - 4x\\sqrt2 = 16 + y^2 + 4y\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7111b885515548861b48cdda99fa34e947203f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - 4x\\sqrt2 = y^2 + 4y\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f7cfe56f23e146e8e7c3deeded652316db44be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - y^2 = 4x\\sqrt2 + 4y\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafe651baed2c8fc9d298453f6cb11bdae26c7f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x + y)(x - y) = (x + y)4\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1834d3cb81b31945211fdccfcc0c833ff618ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x - y = 4\\sqrt2\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b4882b2cd72ba6890e068fb651e4face7be6dccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - y = BC - CD = \\boxed{4\\sqrt2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"218\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071144\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 81/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5032/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37359:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018071144 and revision id 288761. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}